# Hotel PMS UI

Follow **`docs/UI_PLAYBOOK_SATELLITES.md`** and existing hotel patterns (`GuestCardModal`, reservation cards, ElektraWeb-era layouts).

- Use `@era/satellite-kit/ui` primitives where available (`MODAL_INPUT_CLASS`, etc.).
- List grids: `HotelDataGrid` (wraps kit `EraDataGrid` with i18n `ListPaginationFooter`) — not bare `EraDataGrid`.
- Guest identity: support AZ FIN and foreign passport (`GuestCardIdentityTab`).
- If UX conflicts with playbook, follow playbook or ask the user.

## List screens (required)

- Every table/grid page: `PageHeader` -> `EraListFilterBar` (Field*/DatePicker) -> `HotelDataGrid` (or shell+scroll table).
- **Class A (guests, FO reservations):** `LIST_PAGE_SHELL_CLASS` + `EraListWorkspace` + server `{ items, total, page, pageSize }` (25/50/100). Filters go in the query string — not client-only over a dump. Reservations default status filter = **Live** (`OPTION|CONFIRMED|IN_HOUSE`); All is explicit.
- **Class B (catalogs / modals):** client footer on by default (25/50/100); pass `pagination={false}` or `embedded` only for tiny modal lists.
- Table chrome: `DATA_TABLE_SHELL_CLASS` + `DATA_TABLE_SCROLL_CLASS` (or fill scroll inside workspace). Legacy `DATA_TABLE_VIEWPORT_CLASS` ok until migrated.
- CRUD add via modal (`ModalShell` + `Field*`), never `window.prompt`.
- Errors: `showApiError` toast — not inline `text-red-*` / StatusMessage for API failures.
- 3-tier tokens: `docs/adr/era-design-tokens-3tier.md` + `resolveField` / `columnFilters`.
- Guest CRM subpages: `GuestCrmPromptListPage` + `GuestCrmSubnav` layout under `/guests/[id]`.

## Modals (global kit rule)

- `ModalShell` / `EraModal`: backdrop does **not** close on click; no Esc dismiss. Exit only via Close / Cancel / footer buttons.
- While open: `document.body` scroll locked; overlay `pt-10` (not `pt-24`) so near-fullscreen cards fit without page scroll.
- FO cards use `MODAL_FULL_CLASS` (`max-h-[90vh]`).

## Reservation card (near-fullscreen modal)

- **One source** for create and edit: `ReservationCardEditor` via `ReservationCardModal` (`reservationId` null = create). Same panels/tabs always; post-save actions disabled with `availableAfterSave` tooltip.
- One chrome only: `ModalShell` title + `subtitle` (guest · status · id). Do **not** nest a second title/Close toolbar.
- Secondary actions (Menu / Print / Attach / Lightning) → `headerActions`; Save / Check-in → `footer` via `ReservationCardActions`.
- Max width: `MODAL_FULL_CLASS` (~98vw / 1600px). Layout: **50/50** `lg:grid-cols-2` — left form · right collection tabs.
- FO header actions: **Room booking** (single stay card) + **Group booking** (multi-stay wizard). Screen chain (RTA / list / rack / plan) stays in the sidebar, not as header chips.
- Left rail: Stay · Product (room type + Package/rate + meal) · Pax · Classification · Commercial · Assignment (CONFIRMED+) · Additional. No `roomCount` on single card (1 stay = 1 room).
- Right (~60%): tabs Guests · Pricing · Folio · Notes.
- Guests tab = primary/companions grid + party billing PRIMARY/EQUAL. Pricing / Folio / Notes stay as collection tabs.
- Create = edit same chrome; Assignment block hidden on create / pre-arrival OPTION.
- Tabs: kit `TAB_STRIP_CLASS` / `TAB_ITEM_*`; folio subtabs: `CHIP_*`.
- Stay dates: kit `DatePicker` + `common.datePlaceholder` (never native `type="date"` alone).
- Folio grid: `HotelDataGrid`. No raw hex buttons — `SUCCESS_BUTTON_CLASS` / `DANGER_BUTTON_CLASS` / `SECONDARY_BUTTON_CLASS`.

## Guest card (same FO chrome)

- **One source** for create and edit: `GuestCardModal` (`guestId` null = create). Same 50/50 + stats strip (zeros until saved) + left panels + right tabs.
- Same `MODAL_FULL_CLASS` + **50/50** grid. Stats strip above the split.
- Left: static `FieldPanel` groups — Identity · Classification · Documents & MDM · Other. Scalars live left; MDM lookup/merge in Documents panel.
- Right tabs: Identity/Contact (docs/contacts/addresses/consents) · CRM · Reservations · Loyalty · Time share. No separate Details tab.
- Dates via `DatePicker`; fields via kit `Field` / `FieldRow`.

## FO screen chain

Priority: **Room type availability** `/availability` → reservation list → rack `/` → room plan. See `docs/adr/hotel-fo-screen-chain.md`. Empty plan/rack cells = free doors, not sellable Avl.

## Room rack

- `/fo/rack`: From–To `DatePicker` interval (stay overlap); left filter column `overflow-y-auto` and room grid `overflow-y-auto` as separate panes (`LIST_PAGE_SHELL_CLASS`).

## Room plan

- Room plan (`/room-plan`): `EraListFilterBar` Tarix (`DatePicker` → API `from`) + Otaq/Qonaq client filters; grouping/period stay as `FilterMenuButton`; fullscreen overlay like clinic resource matrix (Esc exits).
- Room plan bars (`room-plan/shapes.ts`): half-day (noon) model — box spans mid check-in column → mid check-out column. Right edge = blunt `arrow` (fixed `CHEVRON_PX`, not % of bar width) whenever checkout is in-window; `flat` only when clipped past the window. Left edge = matching EW butt notch for any in-window multi-night start; clipped start stays flat. Geometry is precomputed in `computePlacedBars`; `barSvgPath(flags, widthPx)` builds pixel user-space. Exclusive doors = single lane; share doors = N lanes via `share-lanes.ts` (never paint overlapping stays on the same `top`). Fill = day-state (`plan-bar-theme.ts`); **stroke** = occupancy (exclusive / share M / share F). No HK squares on the plan — OOO/OOS/repair rooms omitted. Two names on the bar when party or overlapping share roommate; guest folio debt badge on the arrow nose. Date header = large day + weekday (EW).
